  body: "# Period of study for entitlement purposes\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured chapter
    gives different IS and JSA meanings for the period of study and expressly confines these definitions
    to entitlement purposes.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe IS course-start-to-end description and
    JSA treated-attendance description must not become a single calendar definition. They do not automatically
    determine student-income periods, loan assessments, holiday eligibility or current course status;
    abandonment, dismissal, connected periods and exceptions require review.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 30218, PDF page 40](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/660bd8e238f66c001184a8db/dmgch30.pdf#page=40)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 30: Students, young claimants and their partners.\n- [DMG 30219, PDF page 40](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/660bd8e238f66c001184a8db/dmgch30.pdf#page=40)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 30: Students, young claimants and their partners.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\
    \nModel-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot.
    Specialist review is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this
    record’s authoring time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted
    text may alter reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage
    or behavioural evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol6-ch30`: PDF SHA-256 `1540b54680884fdaa8a71e26fdebe12899d876b459d448198a7c941a37960780`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `768537aba8259637b2425c4f5359b19a59adee89282078ead1e22f6c4f973665`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/legacy-jsais-student-eligibility
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly connects these definitions to deciding entitlement, rather than
      every use of dates in the student chapter.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch30/0040
      quote: "30218 For entitlement purposes only, the period of study 1 begins on the date that the student
        starts\nattending or undertaking the course and ends on\n\n\n1. the last day of the course or\n\
        \n\n2. such earlier date as the student\n\n\n      2.1 abandons the course or\n\n\n      2.2 is
        dismissed from the course.\n\n\n                                                             \
        \                      1 IS (Gen) Regs, reg 2(1)\n\n\nJSA"
      locator: DMG 30218
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch30/0040
      quote: "30219 For entitlement purposes only, the period of study 1 is\n\n\n1. the period that the
        student is treated as attending or undertaking the course of study and\n\n\n2. any period of attendance
        by the student at their educational establishment or any period of study\nundertaken by a student
        in connection with their course, which is before or after the period of the course.\n\n\n    \
        \                                                                                     1 JSA Regs,
        reg 4\n\n\nNote: The definition at DMG 30218 and DMG 30219 apply to eligibility only. They should
        not be used for\nany other purpose."
      locator: DMG 30219
